 "result": "\n\nSaved `scenario.json` for **G4-CAL-03**.\n\n**Request:** \"Move the Thursday product sync on my main calendar to Conference Room C.\" — one event, identified by title (c1), day (c2, Thursday 2018-06-21), and the actor's primary calendar (c3, `D:primary`, realized via a nested edge `calendar_events → calendars → calendar_list_entries.primary=true`). The action is a PATCH of the event's location.\n\n**Decoys:**\n- `ev_sync_home` — **D:primary, F6**: the same \"Product sync\" at the same Thursday time on the secondary calendar \"Jordan Lee (Home)\", whose name reads as the actor's own calendar (the designated similar-name substitute; caught only if the solver resolves \"main calendar\" by the `primary` flag / 'primary' keyword, not by name).\n- `ev_sync_family` — **D:primary, F0**: the same sync on the plainly different secondary calendar \"Family\".\n- `ev_sync_wed` — **A:Event.start, F7**: a \"Product sync\" on the primary the day before (Wednesday) — nearest value on the wrong side of the day condition (dropping `f_from` selects exactly it).\n- `ev_retro` — **A:Event.summary, F8**: \"Product retrospective\" on the primary that Thursday — a similarly titled meeting sharing the word \"Product\".\n\nBackground records (`ev_dinner`, `ev_1on1`, `ev_dentist`) each fail at least two conditions; all decoys were hand-walked to fail exactly one condition, and each mutation (two REPLACEs, two DROPs) was checked to select its witness while the original query selects only the target.",
